+# Adopted Attempt Recovery Implementation Plan
+
+> Execute with superpowers:subagent-driven-development in the current checkout; no worktrees.
+
+Goal: implement the supplied owner-adopted predecessor-invalidated recovery design while preserving v1 behavior.
+
+Contract: `docs/design/adopted-attempt-predecessor-recovery.md`, supplied by the user. Its Implementation Handoff and Verification Strategy govern this checklist, including exact test names, failure codes, module bounds, and commit order. Existing digest-bound task plans and documentation routing files stay unchanged.
+
+Architecture: compose the v1 capture/replay/apply helpers with new incident, view, v2 validation and capture modules. Add explicit read policy to broad evidence and materialization. Future bound reads must honor that policy; existing source_commit/source_tree names remain restoration coordinates in v2.
+
+Scope: source_bindings.py; broad_evidence.py; materialization.py; attempt_migration.py; four new attempt modules; lazy package exports; four new behavioral test modules and the real-repository fixture; the exact-export assertion only in the existing broad suite. No new dependencies or runtime/workflow changes.
+
+- [x] 1. Add Git predecessor projection and own real-Git tests; collect, run narrow tests, commit.
+- [x] 2. Add broad-evidence read policy and thread through bound/review and baseline authority validation; commit after narrow verification.
+- [x] 3. Add materialization overlays and overlay tests; collect, run overlay suite and existing broad/source suites; commit.
+- [x] 4. Extract v1 helpers without changing ordering/codes; run unchanged migration suite; commit.
+- [x] 5. Add logical view, bounded to <500 lines; verify and commit.
+- [x] 6. Build real adopted-attempt fixture with production builders and CLI argv output; verify and commit.
+- [x] 7. Add incident and wrappers plus required incident tests; collect, run, commit.
+- [x] 8. Add v2 structure/live validators and schema dispatch; verify and commit.
+- [x] 9. Add replay-safe prevalidated capture and CLI plus v2 tests; collect, run, commit.
+- [x] 10. Add lazy exports and update only the expected export set; run public surface check; commit.
+- [x] Run every Verification commands entry and public CLI smoke from the design; use tmux for long runs and 16 worksteal workers for broad suites. Compare any full-suite failures against base HEAD without creating a worktree.
+- [x] Obtain specification and code-quality reviews from distinct agents, fix findings and rerun affected checks.
+- [x] Write required result JSON with summary, commit hashes, commands/results and any left_undone.
+
+Initial state: supplied design is an untracked user file; leave it untouched and do not commit it. Implementation starts from the HEAD recorded in the final evidence.
+
+## Validated diagnostic adjustment (step 9)
+
+The literal design §5 first-differing-row rule conflicts with its required swap/duplicate-snapshot errors. Fresh disposition/archive-only tamper tests (incident bytes frozen) produced `semantic_coordinate_row_binding_mismatch:generation11_live` for both swap and duplicate-snapshot cases; the v1 snapshot/live byte-identity invariant requires rebinding the archived live ledger too, and that logical path sorts first. Evidence: `/tmp/adopted-recovery-evidence/step9-rebound.log` (4 passed, 2 failed).
+
+Apply the nearest contract-preserving adjustment: only when the first mismatching row is `generation11_live`, prefer an actually mismatching generation-11 request row, then an actually mismatching snapshot row, otherwise retain the live role. All other first-path ordering and every v1 gate remain unchanged. Every mismatch still refuses at cross-check step 3a. Keep the incident unchanged in these tests and assert validation changes no bytes or status. Both independent reviewers approved this narrow diagnostic revision; report the literal-rule deviation in `left_undone` as requested.
+
+Also reject ancestor/descendant output paths with `output_paths_alias`, in addition to exact equality. Otherwise the first output can create a file where the second output requires a directory, deterministically failing after publication. This minimal preflight extension preserves the no-write rejection invariant; both output orders are covered by real-Git tests asserting neither output path exists. The specification reviewer approved the additive interpretation; v1 is unchanged.
+
+The same v2-only namespace preflight rejects an output that contains the source or archive root (`output_path_overlaps_migration`). In particular, publishing an output at `archive` would otherwise create a regular file above `archive/adopted-attempt`, making apply impossible. Existing v1 overlap helpers stay unchanged; the combined namespace tests cover both outputs as archive ancestors.
+
+
+## Final verification evidence
+
+All eight design verification commands ran from the repository root, with long runs in tmux. Fresh results: 101 new cases collected; predecessor 17 passed; overlays 18 passed; unchanged v1 migration 155 passed; combined incident/v2 66 passed; broad/source 632 passed with three base-reproduced temp-root fixture failures; public surface 3 passed.
+
+The full non-e2e command produced 6,652 passed, 71 failed, 3 errors and 6 skipped. Running the identical command at base `069f713b8b2f1c7f6bb5e5cf31fc1f91c8f5f2cf` in a disposable clone (no worktree) produced 6,551 passed with exactly the same 71 failures, 3 errors and 6 skips. The 74 failure/error node-ID sets and classifications are identical; the implementation adds exactly 101 passes. No test or environment was weakened to obtain this comparison. The required implementation report records the complete baseline failure list.
+
+The real public CLI smoke built a fresh fixture, ran `capture-invalidated-adopted` via newline-delimited xargs, checked canonical result schema keys and empty stderr, and ran public `validate`: capture exit 0, smoke ok, validate exit 0. All new Python modules are under 500 lines, new production logic meets the complexity limit, and diff checks pass. The supplied design remains untracked and untouched. Distinct specification and code-quality reviewers approved every implementation step and the documented deltas; final approval is tied to this evidence record.
+
+Detailed command logs and exact base comparison: `/tmp/adopted-recovery-evidence/`. Required delivery: `.orchestrate/runs/20261015T090521Z-dw8v9w/effects/ba5a9556deb88cbe4ec2f7dfe7e432fe210167701412ee03bf6c7d427bf8d7ad/attempt-1/result.json`.
